{"format":"hologram.registry.artifact/v1","id":"artifacthub/community-operators/camel-k","fetched":"2026-09-25T12:17:00.609Z","source":{"name":"Artifact Hub","api":"https://artifacthub.io/api/v1/packages/olm/community-operators/camel-k","page":"https://artifacthub.io/packages/olm/community-operators/camel-k"},"readme":"Apache Camel K\n==============\n\nApache Camel K is a lightweight integration platform, born on Kubernetes, with serverless superpowers:\nthe easiest way to build and manage your Camel applications on Kubernetes.\n\n## Installation\n\nProceed to the Camel K operator installation via `Subscription` or via GUI.\nSee official Apache Camel K documentation to learn how to configure all the available parameters.\n\n## Running an Integration\n\nRun a Camel application on the cluster by creating a sample `Integration`, e.g.:\n```\napiVersion: camel.apache.org/v1\nkind: Integration\nmetadata:\n  name: test\nspec:\n  flows:\n  - from:\n      parameters:\n        period: \"1000\"\n      steps:\n      - setBody:\n          simple: Hello Camel from ${routeId}\n      - log: ${body}\n      uri: timer:yaml\n```\nLog the result of the running application:\n```\nkubectl wait --for=condition=ready integration test --timeout=180s\nkubectl logs deployment/test -f\n```","readmeBase":"https://github.com/k8s-operatorhub/community-operators/operators","publisher":{"name":"Operator Framework","url":"https://artifacthub.io/packages/search?org=operator-framework","official":false,"verified":false,"cncf":false},"registered":null,"updated":"2026-09-07T12:45:18.000Z","categories":["Integration and delivery"],"keywords":["apache","kamel","kubernetes","serverless","microservices","Integration & Delivery"],"license":null,"links":[{"name":"Camel K source code repository","url":"https://github.com/apache/camel-k"},{"name":"source","url":"https://github.com/apache/camel-k"},{"name":"Community Operators repository","url":"https://github.com/k8s-operatorhub/community-operators/operators"}]